### 2.7 Vendor & Inventory
**Connected via:** `Inventory.vendor` mapped to `Vendor.name`.

**Vendor Table**:
`name` and `status` are **NOT NULL**. Address, emails and phones are **NULL / BLANK**.

**Inventory Table**:
`name`, `quantity` (Integer) and `unit_price` (Decimal) are **NOT NULL** and strongly demand data. The `category` and `vendor` identifiers accept **NULL / BLANK**.

### 2.8 Tracking
**Tracking** maps `vehicle_number`.
Requires `speed` (Float, Default 0.0) and `status` (**NOT NULL**). `latitude` and `longitude` are natively set to **NULL / BLANK** allowed.

---

> [!NOTE]
> **Summary on Null Types:** 
> Django models in this project heavily utilize implicit relational mapping (string checks instead of SQL strict foreign keys constraints). Fields marked as **NULL / BLANK** can accept empty forms dynamically on the frontend. Fields marked **NOT NULL** will crash the API if not sent with explicit data.
